  </section>
  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Who I Am</h2>
        <p>I am Hassam Shabbir. I hold a B.S. in Psychology from the University of Sargodha, and I have spent 8+ years working across research, writing, and digital strategy. Today I work as a Senior SEO/AEO/GEO Specialist at Quality Resource, where I lead search initiatives across multiple brands, and as a part-time SEO consultant at SARC Med IQ.</p>
        <p>Alongside that work, I have trained more than 400 professionals in AI and prompt engineering, and I founded Rise Above Minds, a nonprofit that teaches digital skills to students. Teaching is what I keep coming back to: taking something complicated and making it clear enough to act on.</p>
        <h2>Why I Built This Site</h2>
        <p>I built Sports Performance Psychology because the field deserved a better resource than what I could find. Too much of what is published about the mental game is either locked behind academic jargon or reduced to empty motivation. I wanted a publication that treats readers like adults: real techniques explained plainly, honest guides to degrees and careers, and figures that come with their sources attached.</p>
        <p>Everything on this site is written by me, in my own words, and checked against the sources I cite. If I am unsure about something, I say so. If I get something wrong, I correct it. That is the deal I am offering you as a reader.</p>
        <h2>An Honest Boundary</h2>
        <p>I am not a licensed clinician, and this site is not clinical advice. I write about mental performance skills for healthy athletes and performers: focus, confidence, routines, visualization. If you are dealing with a mental health concern, please work with a licensed professional. I take this boundary seriously, and so should every publication in this space.</p>
        <h2>Connect With Me</h2>
        <p>You can find me here:</p>
